{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_470e331903969e540e10930219b7073fb196f926befaa3de9e163cf79ff031f0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_873265a1b5770a5adcacf36a4d66008c99a8c91eb93c746fa2de3a7805acc8d7"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"In alpha, LLM Councils support 2–10 distinct models including the main implementer, and each project allows only one active ticket in the execution band at a time.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_69e7b28e17c7c9cd3cb62f6703a31855cef9ef7c7de36dfb200688a37ec3842f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4547b269d4afaa54942dfb6c23792c45a3ecb60e975c979e6db8dac308112ab9","slc_5c6456a19c1a561cd5a32963ca0c4d64307d3f559aae7d3505e20d8e664fb1b0"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"A CLI is provided: `looptroop open` starts the app in the background if not running, and `looptroop start` runs the service without a browser.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_79e8d01bb7cca8c65d5e547819fb6446a45c092360becd077008e0137c17d57b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8ba1c4dc7cd596f2f3cc9c737d561ca3c74e4c72c3d7fae022437aaaa064ab03","slc_9d9c459d403ec64e62f700b9258ad72d0798a8833d43a1a0877cc5ae2afad9fd","slc_b7f726702c7a0d34d273dde9a1d4a20519eb062a59172bcd7bf99bc096d99913"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"Execution runs each bead via OpenCode in isolated Git worktrees; on failure a Ralph-style loop logs the trace, resets the worktree, discards the session, and retries fresh until tests pass or limits are hit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7d72436a35c6911703a34bc27f83f0608d467a48771687b442901d14fabc07a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_275aba1412050d02af059d6813d8ddaf4728a8713a36113b1ba1ad24aa1ea13d","slc_2bb8c3bb13e5d445fd16325a1eba1de3a4befc60bf6820a81630a67acaeb9711","slc_449952528e472867c3b1033a21af1abc273d9aa8f3e2458fcb1305583bdff131","slc_b78b58b72a366be87389f3ac9ff41e862e70dbb5d24e25f81f010e92cd843d20","slc_c7e32b34ef830670e3289a2f646ac4f180e91c7b7dc54a9b81c78834d14868ab"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"A local GUI dashboard lets users manage attached repositories, configure implementer and council models, answer interview questions, and track ticket, bead, and execution-log state.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9ab483c3e8ba2c80a49d5d377d7be79d1c03b30e24c1c0bccbecbcc55fa9273b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f208bd0481c65883e45a3a5648830698d1347630bee617892f1b35000b10bd9"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"The product requires git and authenticated `gh` for the PR step, plus OpenCode with at least one configured model provider; it can start OpenCode if installed but will not install it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b00207897340c2e07835c964b9903801cb62727d88e67234867ff03b7c4abfa9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7bd096d1bab5e581d41b1362f17a67fde8439a95895d627dbfe46f9628170995"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"The tool is unsuited to urgent quick fixes or trivial tasks due to orchestration overhead and high API token usage from multi-model councils and long retry loops.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bf135ab44661ce02e9ae835846df128830396284bf74cd08c16cea3085d647dd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_75c2e75615d770a7c106eac482237903cc9684e67a477170505d8d67c3d097d0","slc_9741b4fbfa7eb0ee9d1c0b9df20f3a62dcc3840be75116c051750b4ab5bbadd3","slc_ebda794e8dfbdbfb49bd7601e2c129b5e065b9cc2a2253078462ac51ab8e3107","slc_f7a98a5b910968e74975d5c010c7472ace42ca7c9cbe8ef25c602b4d33c84dd2"],"source_ids":["src_72139a2ae8ef55e7ae706ff88aab3779"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run `npm install` and `npm run dev` (dev server at localhost:5173), with lint, typecheck, and test scripts available, and a preview mode serving a built bundle.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c4cd945265732b7bb583c43f88fd873886f55696f36a2fd3be84af724c406f56","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_23e18938d8a32ec055b9fcc7398c464a060708ff7f75854f75c1a7c85eec7784","slc_b16c735c4c3c1ef64767bbb7531638f1b6df6ec558e02f6ac03225706f4cd5fd"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"The orchestrator runs OpenCode in dangerously-skip-permissions (YOLO) mode, giving the agent full local execution rights without confirmation prompts; worktrees isolate code but not command execution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ccbe11c3fcb65bc48edc088b700798cf7c05da855c8c14a1f98e4125da75fadd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"looptroop-ai/looptroop@b96f5448251c snapshot 3f7a06becba16b57","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_503b8a33f121d45bc0a4152f41acb7cbbcaef418e77091ddbb8287ef6f90f3bd","slc_b8d24ab8b4eb881429ea7843f90a35383b8005bae76c5f42baca42275788434b","slc_c7334c9a1f6227de2388250cc23d944fcf89095e6577943697cb8d135ec20453","slc_d0d68688b28694f0482ce9f5eb30470762a0979f0610f11b3a5c7552e5d854b9"],"source_ids":["src_bf994b4b089651d099914dc939c3245b"],"text":"npm/bun/pnpm/Yarn installs need Node 24.18.1+ and git and gh; Homebrew and Scoop ship locked bundles pulling in node@24, git, and gh; Docker images include Node, git, and gh but need an external OpenCode server and a mounted project.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:13:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3a12e625a6614eb38a44c43b260697e5"}
